", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction to the description (2026-11-09 15:20 PST): the harness does NOT exit on this error. The 12:21 PST run (pid 27240) printed the 'cannot list .tickets-tracker' line and kept running, making model calls for 3 hours. The error is a non-fatal line on stderr, so the observed defect is a misleading error message emitted before the run proceeds, not an aborted run. Which call emits it is still untraced. The reproduction steps showing a second run proceeding after a CLI call are unaffected; the claim that the first run stopped was wrong.","timestamp":1794266176936456001}],"created_at":1794258352458117001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"af3aa9d7-e9c8-4aeb-9681-3c963eef485b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7341-7f22-b13a-442c"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity` (the operator-run parity harness) fails immediately in a fresh worktree created by `make worktree`:\n\n```\nError: cannot list '<worktree>/.tickets-tracker': [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '<worktree>/.tickets-tracker'\n```\n\nNo model call is made and the run exits before writing any result.\n\n## Reproduction (measured 2026-11-09, origin/main 872e7f6c3fd)\n\n1. `make worktree name=eval-baseline-4x` from the main checkout.\n2. In that worktree, with no prior `rebar` CLI call: `env AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock .venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity --concurrency 4 --out <path>` prints the error above and stops.\n3. Run any tracker read, e.g. `.venv/bin/rebar show <id>`. It creates the `.tickets-tracker` symlink to the shared tracker.\n4. Re-run step 2's command with `--dry-run`: it lists the 50-item corpus and proceeds.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe harness attaches (or resolves) the tracker the same way the CLI does on its first command, or fails with an error naming the remedy. It should not depend on an unrelated earlier CLI call having run in that worktree.\n\n## Notes\n\nFound while running the before/after provider-parity evals for the model upgrade. The harness enters `gate_source.gate_read_root(handle)` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py:355`); which call lists the tracker directory was not traced.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4e0a-0d78-ecac-4656","ticket_type":"bug","title":"provider_parity harness fails in a fresh worktree until a CLI call attaches .tickets-tracker","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3b175bc5-791d-4c7e-a2ea-3f70203775ce","af3aa9d7-e9c8-4aeb-9681-3c963eef485b","6ea5aa32-ed3c-44e6-9251-b37f4febc3a8"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794266176936456002,"uuid":"ff599a71-79fa-431b-9d55-31a1795cca0f"}